    "inspection": "Inspected the official 2025–2026 regulations and student handbook through indexed copies. Article 3.3.2 refers thesis load and requirements to the prospectus. The handbook describes final-semester automatic enrolment at 120 EC for that edition. Neither establishes the 2029 class allocation or progression. Targeted 2026–2027 regulations and grid requests returned access blocks or yielded only prior editions in official search. The result does not show that no applicable rules exist."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Current annual degree and CHS payloads were obtained. Nominal 2027–2028 and 2028–2029 requests returned byte-identical 2026–2027 material. The CHS product names the 40 EC choice block and 15 EC capstone for class of 2028 and the 45 EC choice block and 10 EC capstone for classes of 2026 and 2027. It does not identify a 2029 rule.",
    "The current route groups name Capstone Thesis, 26–27 (8004CS001Y). The module endpoint returns JSON null at all three queried years. The label supplies neither the September 2026 entrant credit load nor its progression conditions. Adjacent majors that use onwards in their cohort labels cannot establish the CHS rule.",
    "The verified seven compulsory first-year components still total 45 EC. The three UCR schedules, workbook-based course contribution review and all 33 interest rows remain reusable."
  ],
  "unresolved": "Confirm the official Culture, History and Society major requirements for September 2026 entrants (expected class of 2029), specifically the capstone credits, remaining major-course credits and thesis progression. The 2026–2027 catalogue labels the 15 EC version for class of 2028 only and the 10 EC version for classes of 2026 and 2027.",
  "retryDisposition": "Second unsuccessful essential-source execution. Preserve the 45 EC partial curriculum and existing UCR work. Operational deferral follows published evidence and CI verification. Separate revisit unused."
